a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1133" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="7A9BB5"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:rPr><a:t>Higher  NFZ → higher minimum flyable altitude → longer 3D paths even when horizontal routing is similar.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="171450" indent="-171450" defTabSz="1219170"><a:buFont typeface="Arial" panose="020B0604020202020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1133" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="7A9BB5"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:rPr><a:t>Vertical lift at OD dominates the gap between shortest and total paths; it grows predictably with ground clearance.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="171450" indent="-171450" defTabSz="1219170"><a:buFont typeface="Arial" panose="020B0604020202020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1133" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="7A9BB5"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:rPr><a:t>Also limited paths are available as  NFZ increases hence aircraft needs to fly even higher.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="171450" indent="-171450" defTabSz="1219170"><a:buFont typeface="Arial" panose="020B0604020202020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1133" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="7A9BB5"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:rPr><a:t>Path topology (which corners are used) is similar across pairs; sensitivity is mainly altitude / length, not failure to find a path.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="171450" indent="-171450" defTabSz="1219170"><a:buFont typeface="Arial" panose="020B0604020202020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1133" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="7A9BB5"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:rPr><a:t>Operational implication: clearance is a first-order parameter for UAM routes from surface vertiports.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="171450" indent="-171450" defTabSz="1219170"><a:buFont typeface="Arial" panose="020B0604020202020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1133" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="7A9BB5"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="171450" indent="-171450" defTabSz="1219170"><a:buFont typeface="Arial" panose="020B0604020202020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1133" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="7A9BB5"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-122"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri" pitchFamily="34" charset="-120"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="171450" indent="-171450" defTabSz="1219170"><a:buFont typeface="Arial" panose="020B0604020202020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1133" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="7A9BB5"/></a:soli